          "en": "this screen onto the stack of screens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 322.08,
          "end": 325.29,
          "en": "but instead you replace the currently active screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 325.29,
          "end": 326.85,
          "en": "with the FiltersScreen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 326.85,
          "end": 329.01,
          "en": "so that the back button would not work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 329.01,
          "end": 330.633,
          "en": "and would not take you back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 331.5,
          "end": 333.75,
          "en": "And since this is also a pattern you should know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 333.75,
          "end": 336.72,
          "en": "I'm also going to show you how this could be implemented.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 336.72,
          "end": 338.7,
          "en": "Because it's really straightforward to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 338.7,
          "end": 340.83,
          "en": "You just replace push, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 340.83,
          "end": 344.58299999999997,
          "en": "here in the TabsScreen file, with pushReplacement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 345.69,
          "end": 348.06,
          "en": "And the rest stays as it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 348.06,
          "end": 351.69,
          "en": "But this will now make sure that FiltersScreen is not pushed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 351.69,
          "end": 354.51,
          "en": "as a new screen onto the stack of screens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 354.51,
          "end": 357.09000000000003,
          "en": "but that instead the currently active screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 357.09000000000003,
          "end": 360.03,
          "en": "in this case TabsScreen will be replaced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 360.03,
          "end": 361.83,
          "en": "with the FiltersScreen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 361.83,
          "end": 364.17,
          "en": "And therefore, the back button wouldn't work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 364.17,
          "end": 367.68,
          "en": "because there is nowhere to go back to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 367.68,
          "end": 370.26,
          "en": "And you can do the same in the FiltersScreen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 370.26,
          "end": 374.4,
          "en": "There, when you navigate to the TabsScreen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 374.4,
          "end": 378.57,
          "en": "you could use pushReplacement instead of push.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 378.57,
          "end": 383.28,
          "en": "If you make those changes and you restart your app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 383.28,
          "end": 386.52,
          "en": "you will see that the drawer still works as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 386.52,
          "end": 388.8,
          "en": "But if I go to the FiltersScreen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 388.8,
          "end": 391.83,
          "en": "and I then press the back button, I actually close the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 391.83,
          "end": 394.44,
          "en": "because there was no screen to go back to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 394.44,
          "end": 398.34000000000003,
          "en": "And then the default behavior indeed is to close the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 398.34000000000003,
          "end": 400.98,
          "en": "So that's simply an alternative navigation pattern,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 400.98,
          "end": 403.17,
          "en": "which you should also be aware of,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
